  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you are responsible for migrating a large Oracle Database to Google Cloud Spanner while ensuring minimal downtime and maintaining a fallback plan. Choose the best migration strategy for this scenario.",
  "originalOptions": "A. Utilize the Schema Conversion Tool (SCT) to convert the Oracle schema for Spanner, perform data transfer using Dataflow, and set up a Cloud SQL instance with an Oracle database as a fallback.<br/>B. Use Google Cloud Datastore to import the Oracle schema and data, then create a Datastore export as a fallback plan.<br/>C. Create a Spanner instance, use the Cloud Spanner import functionality to convert the schema and transfer data, and set up a reverse replication from Spanner to the on-premises Oracle database as a fallback.<br/>D. Utilize the Schema Conversion Tool (SCT) to convert the Oracle schema for Spanner, perform data transfer using Datastream, and set up a reverse replication from Spanner to the on-premises Oracle database as a fallback.",
